THE DATA FILES IN `embedded/`

Apache-2.0 covers the software in this repository. It does not cover
these data files, which are the work of other bodies and keep their
own status. They are listed here so that status travels with them.

`embedded/antennas/` and `embedded/database/`, about 16 KB, are part
of the VOACAP distribution and carry the NTIA/ITS status above.

`embedded/coeffs/` holds 544 KB in thirteen files: twelve monthly
files and the CCIR foF2 map. Two bodies wrote what is inside them.
The split below is measured by the arrays `REDMAP` reads, record by
record, and rounded:

    195 KB   Sporadic-E, E region and F1 maps, the F2 height ratio,
             the solar index table and the prediction error
             statistics. NTIA/ITS work, same status as the antenna
             files above.

    216 KB   Atmospheric radio noise: Fam, its variability and the
             related maps. From CCIR Report 322.

    134 KB   The foF2 and M(3000)F2 ionospheric maps. From CCIR
             Report 340.

The ITU publishes the CCIR Report 322 and Report 340 data itself, in
the reference software of ITU-R Study Group 3 for Recommendations
P.372 and P.533, at github.com/ITU-R-Study-Group-3/ITU-R-HF, with this
statement:

    The ITURHFProp, P533 and P372 software has been developed
    collaboratively by participants in ITU-R Study Group 3. It may be
    used by implementers in their implementation of the Recommendation
    as well as in revisions of the specific original Recommendation and
    in other ITU Recommendations, free from any copyright assertions.

The files here come through the VOACAP distribution rather than
through the ITU's own release, so they hold the same coefficient set
in a different binary format. `docs/licence.md` records what was
compared, and what this arrangement does and does not settle.

The URSI-88 foF2 maps, which VOACAP reads for a `COEFFS URSI88` card,
are not in this repository. They are the one part of the coefficient
set that the ITU does not publish itself. `COEFFS URSI88` therefore
needs a real `itshfbc` tree.

The published crate on crates.io carries none of `embedded/coeffs/`.
Those files are behind the `embedded-coefficients` feature, which is
off by default and excluded from the package.


OTHER SOFTWARE THIS PRODUCT DOES NOT INCLUDE

The comparisons in `docs/engines.md` drive the ITU-R Study Group 3
reference implementation of Recommendation P.533. That software is not
included here and is not part of this product.

The `voacapl` distribution contains two GPL-3.0 programs, `dst2csv.f90`
and `dst2ascii.f90`. Neither is included here, and nothing in this
product derives from them or from the `f90getopt` module they use.
